Article translation migration

Article translations use domain contracts, an injected AI interface, authenticated HTTP adapters, and atomic locale updates. Client requests validate responses and cancel stale work. The migration preserves four-locale saved sentence cards and summary endpoint behavior.

Verification: 95 focused tests passed, including PostgreSQL concurrency. Source typechecks passed. Focused lint passed with 25 legacy application warnings. Tests ran sequentially with a 1536 MB Node heap limit. The disposable database was removed.

Limits: Chapter cache writes still need migration. Final content access policy, browser behavior, and live provider quality remain pending. Chapter helper regression tests followed extraction without a confirmed RED run.

